WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:08.592
This walkthrough connects Slack, so every report, the daily scorecard and reminders post straight into your channels. It takes about three minutes.

00:00:08.792 --> 00:00:14.923
Open the Slack apps page from the link in the guide. Press Create New App, and choose From scratch.

00:00:15.123 --> 00:00:20.785
Give the app a name, such as EOD Reports. Pick your workspace, and press Create App.

00:00:20.985 --> 00:00:30.658
In the left menu, open OAuth and Permissions. Scroll to Bot Token Scopes and add these four: chat write, chat write public, channels read, and groups read.

00:00:30.858 --> 00:00:37.821
Scroll back to the top of that page and press Install to Workspace. Slack asks for permission. Press Allow.

00:00:38.021 --> 00:00:43.854
You now have a Bot User OAuth Token. It starts with xoxb. Press Copy.

00:00:44.054 --> 00:00:51.465
On the settings page, paste it into the Bot token box and press Save Slack. Then press Connect and load channels.

00:00:51.665 --> 00:01:01.167
The boxes turn into lists of your real channels. Pick where each report should go, press Save Slack again, then press Send test messages and check your channels.

00:01:01.367 --> 00:01:10.272
One last thing. If a channel is private, the app cannot post there until you invite it. In that channel, type /invite, followed by your app name.

00:01:10.472 --> 00:01:19.291
That is Slack connected. Reports post as they are filed, the daily scorecard posts on its own, and reminders chase anyone who has not filed.
